---
layout: default
---
{%- comment -%}
  LOCAL SHADOW of al_folio_core's _layouts/cv.liquid (gem v1.0.15).

  Why this file exists
  --------------------
  The gem's version builds the whole page from `{% al_folio_cv_render %}` and
  never emits `{{ content }}`. That means the body of _pages/cv.md is silently
  discarded: no error, no warning, the page just renders without it. Three
  includes in that file had never once appeared on the live site because of it:

      cv_contact_extra.liquid   the LinkedIn row in Contact Information
      linkedin_badge.liquid     the profile badge every other page carries
      goatcounter.liquid        pageview tracking, so /cv/ was untracked

  The only change below is the `{{ content }}` line after the render tag.
  Everything else is copied verbatim from the gem so that behaviour, feature
  gating and the fallback branch stay identical.

  AGENTS.md permits this: the stop-sign paths apply to the al-folio template
  repo itself, and line 36 states that a user's own site "may legally shadow
  gem-owned files". See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, "local overrides: your site vs.
  this repo".

  Maintenance cost, stated plainly
  --------------------------------
  This file is now yours. Upstream fixes to the CV layout will NOT reach it,
  and `bundle exec al-folio upgrade audit` will report it as an override to
  acknowledge (`upgrade overrides diff _layouts/cv.liquid`, then `accept`).
  On any al_folio_core upgrade, re-diff against the gem's copy:

      bundle exec al-folio upgrade overrides diff _layouts/cv.liquid

  If upstream ever adds `{{ content }}` itself, delete this file entirely.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% assign cv_feature_enabled = site.al_folio.features.cv.enabled | default: true %}

{% if site.plugins contains 'al_folio_cv' and cv_feature_enabled %}
  {% al_folio_cv_render %}
  {{ content }}
{% else %}
  <div class="post">
    <header class="post-header">
      <h1 class="post-title">{{ page.title }}</h1>
      <p class="post-description">CV rendering is unavailable.</p>
    </header>
    <article>
      <p>Enable the <code>al_folio_cv</code> plugin and set <code>al_folio.features.cv.enabled: true</code> to render this page.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
{% endif %}
